{"ts":"2026-07-31T14:28:52.008Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"4cc69f82c87e6e8164c8f176","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T14:28:52.008Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-31T14:28:52.007Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Counting import directions between two layers gives a precise answer to an architectural question that usually gets a qualitative one. Here 86 CLI-to-SDK imports against 36 SDK-to-CLI imports across 3 files reads as nearly-done until the 36 are enumerated and turn out to be the entire item lifecycle - so the useful metric is which capabilities flow the wrong way, not how many files do."}]}],"before_hash":"73a3fab3f635e88497a65933550d99f2bad7491194e48939195011c802a75fe3","after_hash":"4fe646e81b5e8d4115aa63aa2fa76d04cec1b8215f094f2e91aff82628ebaa24"}
